1
00:06:05,454 --> 00:06:11,454
His people needed a leader. He gave them a champion.

2
00:12:10,909 --> 00:12:16,909
Invictus is a drama, history film directed by Clint Eastwood.

3
00:18:16,363 --> 00:18:22,363
Newly elected President Nelson Mandela knows his nation remains
racially and economically divided in the wake of apartheid.

4
00:24:21,818 --> 00:24:27,818
Believing he can bring his people together through the universal language of sport, Mandela rallies South Africa's
rugby union team as they make their historic run to the 1995 Rugby World Cup Championship match.

5
00:30:27,272 --> 00:30:33,272
Nelson Mandela, played by Morgan Freeman.

6
00:36:32,727 --> 00:36:38,727
Francois Pienaar, played by Matt Damon.

7
00:42:38,181 --> 00:42:44,181
Jason Tshabalala, played by Tony Kgoroge.

8
00:48:43,636 --> 00:48:49,636
Linga Moonsamy, played by Patrick Mofokeng.

9
00:54:49,090 --> 00:54:55,090
Hendrick Booyens, played by Matt Stern.

10
01:00:54,545 --> 01:01:00,545
Etienne Feyder, played by Julian Lewis Jones.

11
01:07:00,000 --> 01:07:06,000
Invictus is a 2009 docudrama sports film directed by Clint
Eastwood and starring Morgan Freeman and Matt Damon.

12
01:13:05,454 --> 01:13:11,454
It is the third collaboration between Eastwood and Freeman after Unforgiven (1992) and Million Dollar
Baby (2004), and the first between Eastwood and Damon, followed by Hereafter (2010).

13
01:19:10,909 --> 01:19:16,909
The story is based on the 2008 John Carlin book Playing the Enemy: Nelson Mandela and the Game That Made
a Nation about the events in South Africa before and during the 1995 Rugby World Cup.

14
01:25:16,363 --> 01:25:22,363
The national team, the Springboks, were not expected to perform well, the team having only recently returned to high-level international
competition following the dismantling of apartheid—the country was hosting the World Cup, thus earning an automatic entry.

15
01:31:21,818 --> 01:31:27,818
Freeman portrays South African President Nelson Mandela while Damon played Francois
Pienaar, the captain of the Springboks, the South Africa rugby union team.

16
01:37:27,272 --> 01:37:33,272
Invictus was released in the United States on 11 December 2009.

17
01:43:32,727 --> 01:43:38,727
The film is named after a poem of the same name by British poet William Ernest
Henley, which serves as a central plot element in the film.

18
01:49:38,181 --> 01:49:44,181
The film was met with positive critical reviews and earned Academy Award
nominations for Freeman (Best Actor) and Damon (Best Supporting Actor).

19
01:55:43,636 --> 01:55:49,636
The film grossed $122.2 million on a budget of $50–60 million.

20
02:01:49,090 --> 02:01:55,090
The film explores themes of sports, stadium, south africa, apartheid, idealism.

21
02:07:54,545 --> 02:08:00,545
The tone is emotional.
